{"availability":"available","full":"Ksirailway-base/BookMind","name":"BookMind","description":"Offline RAG study assistant powered by LFM2-2.6B · Ask questions, get exercises from any PDF textbook · No cloud required","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-03-21T15:48:06Z","updated":"2026-04-20T14:51:29Z","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["bm25","chroma","education","english-grammar","gradio","langchain","langchain-python","language-learning","lfm2","llama-cpp","llm","llm-inference","local-ai","local-llm","offline-ai","ollama","pdf","python","rag","study-assistant"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Ksirailway/BookMind","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:14.605Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:14.605Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:14.605Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:34:14.605Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Offline RAG assistant for studying with text-based PDF textbooks. Powered with LFM2-2.6B on board. LFM2 is Liquid AI's hybrid architecture — efficient enough to run on RAM-only machines without a GPU. This project is my first test of LFM2 in a real RAG pipeline, with plans to explore its limits on low-power local servers. More LFM2 experiments coming. Upload a book, ask questions, get answers with page references. Everything runs locally via llama.cpp. Optionally switch to OpenAI or Gemini via API key."],"features":["This project is officially featured in the Liquid4All Cookbook as a comprehensive example of a complex RAG application built with Liquid AI models.","Conversational Memory: Implements a Two-Tier Summary Buffer. It keeps the last 12 messages \"hot\" (word-for-word) and automatically compresses older history into a lightweight summary block (extracting discussed topics…","Smart Chunking: PyMuPDF loader with 1800-char chunks and 500-char overlap. Optimized to capture Word Banks and exercise instructions together.","Retrieve & Rank: Two-stage RAG pipeline. Initial Hybrid Search followed by a Cross-Encoder Reranker (MiniLM-L6) to ensure the highest semantic accuracy.","Exercise Generator: Automatically extracts grammar exercises from textbook pages. No hallucinations — exercises are taken directly from the book with all provided options/word banks."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Ksirailway-base/BookMind/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"24ddd32e3e0cbc421049b5b9830aa2652cfe120484527c5114b2b74d400a4621","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:14.743Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:14.743Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Offline RAG assistant for studying with text-based PDF textbooks. Powered with LFM2-2.6B on board. LFM2 is Liquid AI's hybrid architecture — efficient enough to run on RAM-only machines without a GPU. This project is my first test of LFM2 in a real RAG pipeline, with plans to explore its limits on low-power local servers. More LFM2 experiments coming. Upload a book, ask questions, get answers with page references. Everything runs locally via llama.cpp. Optionally switch to OpenAI or Gemini via API key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Ksirailway-base/BookMind/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","text":"Optionally switch to OpenAI or Gemini via API key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Ksirailway-base/BookMind/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"24ddd32e3e0cbc421049b5b9830aa2652cfe120484527c5114b2b74d400a4621","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Ksirailway-base/BookMind/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:14.744Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-04-20T14:51:29Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Ksirailway-base/BookMind/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:14.744Z","hash":"24ddd32e3e0cbc421049b5b9830aa2652cfe120484527c5114b2b74d400a4621","originalBytes":6424,"storedBytes":642